{title: Come, Ye Disconsolate}
{key: F}
{tempo: 69}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: author Thomas Moore}
{meta: author Thomas Hastings}
{meta: author Samuel Webbe}
{meta: year 1816}
{meta: died 1852}
{meta: died 1872}
{meta: died 1816}
{meta: source WorshipCommons, https://worshipcommons.org/songs/RmcfAcbelTI}
{copyright: Public domain}

Verse 1
[F]Come, ye discon[Bb]solate, wher[F]e'er ye [C]languish;
[F]come to the [Dm]mercy seat, [Gm]fervently [C]kneel.
[F]Here bring your [Bb]wounded hearts, [F]here tell your [C]anguish;
[F]earth has no [Bb]sorrow that [C]heaven cannot [F]heal.

Verse 2
Joy of the desolate, light of the straying,
Hope of the penitent, fadeless and pure,
Here speaks the Comforter, tenderly saying,
"Earth has no sorrow that Heav'n cannot cure."

Verse 3
Here see the Bread of Life; see waters flowing
Forth from the throne of God, pure from above;
Come to the feast of love; come, ever knowing
Earth has no sorrow but Heav'n can remove.
